    "Fasted-state, formulation, and food effects can cause variability for this type of molecule; C22 illustrates this but is not threshold-specific.",
    "No affirmative threshold-relevant evidence supports F < 20% for a structurally relevant analog."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high. Transferable L1 absolute F measurements for close anthranilic acid analogs (diclofenac ~50%, tolfenamic acid ~91-100%), sulfonamide celecoxib (20-40%), and carboxylic acid drugs (telmisartan 42-58%, rigosertib ~35%) support F >= 20%. New L2 records are mostly supportive; C22 is qualitative and not threshold-specific. The physicochemical low prior is insufficient to override measured analog outcomes. Confidence is moderate because no direct query F measurement is available."
}

